  <title>Restore an earlier version of a file or folder</title>
  <desc>Find an old version in Files, preview it, and put it back without losing anything.</desc>

  <steps>
    <item>
      <p>In <app>Files</app>, right-click the file or folder and choose <gui style="menuitem">Restore Previous Version…</gui>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>The <gui>Previous versions</gui> window lists every different version, newest first, with when it was backed up and
      its size. Identical copies are shown once.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>Select a version to preview it. Images, text, video and audio show in the window. A big file asks first:
      choose <gui style="button">Show preview</gui>. Anything else opens in its own application with
      <gui style="button">Open</gui>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>Choose how to bring it back:</p>
      <list>
        <item><p><gui style="button">Restore as a copy</gui> puts the old version next to the original, named like
        <file>report (restored 2026-11-16).odt</file>. Nothing is overwritten.</p></item>
        <item><p><gui style="button">Replace the current version…</gui> puts the old version in place of the current one.
        Delta asks first and keeps the current one beside it, renamed with the date and time. If something fails,
        the original goes back to its place.</p></item>
      </list>
    </item>
  </steps>

  <note style="tip">
    <p>If the window says <em>No earlier versions</em>, the item is not in any backup yet.</p>
  </note>

  <section id="folders">
    <title>Folders</title>
    <p>For a folder, the window shows what it held in the version you chose. Open subfolders to move around;
    <gui style="button">Back</gui> goes up.</p>
    <list>
      <item><p><gui>Search by name</gui> finds a file at any depth below the folder.</p></item>
      <item><p>The filter has <gui>All</gui>, <gui>Changed</gui> (everything that differs from your disk now) and
      <gui>Deleted</gui>. Each row says <gui>Modified</gui>, <gui>Changed inside</gui>, <gui>Unchanged</gui> or
      <gui>Deleted</gui>.</p></item>
      <item><p><gui style="button">Select several items</gui> lets you restore many at once.</p></item>
      <item><p><gui style="button">Restore deleted…</gui> puts back everything that was deleted from the folder since
      that version. Nothing that exists today is touched.</p></item>
      <item><p><gui>Show in Files</gui> opens the original location.</p></item>
    </list>
  </section>

  <section id="keys">
    <title>Keyboard</title>
    <list>
      <item><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>F</key></keyseq>: go to the search box.</p></item>
      <item><p><keyseq><key>Alt</key><key>←</key></keyseq>: up one folder, or back from a file to the list.</p></item>
      <item><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>↓</key></keyseq> and <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>↑</key></keyseq>:
      the next older and newer version.</p></item>
      <item><p><key>Esc</key>: clear the search, or leave selection mode.</p></item>
    </list>
  </section>
